From 7bfc9f176678bfc05e5b8425a99865eefd07a9c5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Craig Johnson <1545411+captainpacket@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 18 Jul 2026 08:15:24 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 5/9] vtep: explicit HOST_INTF wins for source selection,
 plugin and daemon
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Routed clusters can carry the Kubernetes hostIP on an interface that is not
the one fabric traffic must use (e.g. a tunnel). The old getVxlanSource
only honoured HOST_INTF if it stumbled on it while scanning addresses, and
returned whatever address family it hit first.

- plugin getVxlanSource: an explicit HOST_INTF now short-circuits — resolve
  the interface's first non-loopback IPv4 address and use it as the VTEP
  source; HOST_IP scanning remains the fallback.
- meshnetd Get: resolve the same way (nodeSource) before answering pod
  queries, so NodeIp/NodeIntf handed to the plugin already reflect the
  configured source interface; falls back to HOST_IP with a warning when
  the interface cannot be resolved.

Upstreamable.
---
